The rewritten program behaves like the IR-mutated one: same mutants, same exit status and output

RUN: rm -rf %S/Output && mkdir -p %S/Output/sandbox
RUN: cp %S/main.cpp %S/mull.yml %S/Output/sandbox/
RUN: cd %S/Output/sandbox && %clang_cxx %sysroot -O0 -g -grecord-command-line %pass_mull_ir_frontend main.cpp -o %S/Output/ir.exe
RUN: cd %S/Output/sandbox && %mull_runner --dry-run --allow-surviving --reporters SQLite --report-dir %S/Output --report-name dry %S/Output/ir.exe
RUN: echo '[{"directory": "%S/Output/sandbox", "file": "main.cpp", "command": "%clang_cxx %sysroot -c main.cpp"}]' > %S/Output/sandbox/compile_commands.json

RUN: %mull_rewriter --report %S/Output/dry.sqlite -p %S/Output/sandbox --root %S/Output/sandbox --output-dir %S/Output/rewritten | %filecheck %s --check-prefix=REWRITER
REWRITER-NOT: Not rewritten
REWRITER: Rewrote {{[0-9]+}} of {{[0-9]+}} mutants in 1 files

RUN: %clang_cxx %sysroot -O0 %S/Output/rewritten/main.cpp -o %S/Output/rewritten.exe
RUN: cd %S/Output/sandbox && %mull_runner --allow-surviving -minimum-timeout 2000 --reporters SQLite --report-dir %S/Output --report-name ir %S/Output/ir.exe
RUN: cd %S/Output/sandbox && %mull_runner --allow-surviving -minimum-timeout 2000 --reporters SQLite --report-dir %S/Output --report-name rewritten %S/Output/rewritten.exe

Every mutant is rewritten
RUN: %sqlite3 %S/Output/ir.sqlite "ATTACH '%S/Output/rewritten.sqlite' AS r; SELECT 'MISSING', mutant_id FROM mutant WHERE mutant_id NOT IN (SELECT mutant_id FROM r.mutant);" | %filecheck %s --allow-empty --check-prefix=MISSING
MISSING-NOT: MISSING

Timeouts are left out: their output depends on when they are killed, and under load a slow mutant
can time out in one program only
RUN: %sqlite3 %S/Output/ir.sqlite "ATTACH '%S/Output/rewritten.sqlite' AS r; SELECT 'DIFF', i.mutator FROM mutant i JOIN r.mutant m USING (mutant_id) WHERE i.execution_status != 3 AND m.execution_status != 3 AND (i.execution_status != m.execution_status OR i.exit_status != m.exit_status OR i.stdout != m.stdout) ORDER BY 2;" | %filecheck %s --check-prefix=DIFF

Known bug: the IR mutants turn '<<' into a logical shift, '>>' on a signed value is arithmetic
DIFF: DIFF|cxx_lshift_assign_to_rshift_assign
DIFF-NEXT: DIFF|cxx_lshift_to_rshift
DIFF-NOT: DIFF
